```

## Expected Test Results

### ✅ Success Patterns

**Connection Test**:
```
✅ Connected to wss://juno-cloud-backend.fly.dev/ws
✅ WebSocket connection successful
✅ Server is responsive
```

**Authentication Test**:
```
✅ Authentication successful
✅ HMAC signature validated
✅ Device registered with cloud
```

**Command Test**:
```
✅ Command sent successfully
✅ Response received from agent
✅ Command processing completed
```

### ❌ Failure Patterns

**Connection Failures**:
```
❌ ECONNREFUSED: Connection refused
❌ ENOTFOUND: DNS resolution failed
❌ Timeout: Server not responding
```

**Authentication Failures**:
```
❌ Invalid API key
❌ HMAC signature mismatch
❌ Authentication timeout
```

**Command Failures**:
```
❌ Command timeout (no response)
❌ Invalid command format
❌ Agent execution error
```

## Performance Benchmarks

### Connection Metrics
- **Connection Time**: < 2 seconds
- **Authentication Time**: < 1 second
- **Command Response Time**: < 30 seconds
- **Reconnection Time**: < 5 seconds

### Success Rate Targets
- **Connection Success**: > 95%
- **Authentication Success**: > 99%
- **Command Success**: > 90%
- **Reconnection Success**: > 85%

## Integration Testing Checklist

Before deploying cloud functionality:

- [ ] ✅ **Basic Connection**: WebSocket connects to cloud server
- [ ] ✅ **Authentication**: API key and HMAC validation work
- [ ] ✅ **Command Sending**: Commands reach cloud backend
- [ ] ✅ **Command Processing**: Commands reach Juno AI agent
- [ ] ✅ **Response Handling**: Agent responses return to client
- [ ] ✅ **Error Handling**: Failures are handled gracefully
- [ ] ✅ **Reconnection**: Auto-reconnection works after failures
- [ ] ✅ **Performance**: Response times meet targets
- [ ] ✅ **Stability**: No memory leaks or crashes
- [ ] ✅ **Compilation**: All code compiles without errors

## Troubleshooting Decision Tree

```
Cloud Connection Issue
│
├── Compilation Error?
│   ├── Yes → Check imports in [src/lib/cloud-connector.ts](mdc:src/lib/cloud-connector.ts)
│   └── No → Continue
│
├── Connection Refused?
│   ├── Yes → Check server URL in config files
│   └── No → Continue
│
├── Authentication Failed?
│   ├── Yes → Verify API key and HMAC secret
│   └── No → Continue
│
├── Commands Not Working?
│   ├── Yes → Test with [call-agent.js](mdc:websocket-test/call-agent.js)
│   └── No → Continue
│
└── Status Shows "Reconnecting"?
    ├── Yes → Check network connectivity and server status
    └── No → Check application logs
```

## Monitoring & Alerting

### Key Metrics to Monitor
```typescript
interface CloudHealthMetrics {
  connectionUptime: number;        // Percentage uptime
  averageResponseTime: number;     // Milliseconds
  commandSuccessRate: number;      // Percentage
  reconnectionFrequency: number;   // Per hour
  errorRate: number;              // Errors per minute
}
```

### Alert Thresholds
- **Connection Uptime** < 95%: Warning
- **Response Time** > 30s: Warning
- **Success Rate** < 90%: Critical
- **Error Rate** > 5/min: Critical

---

**Remember**: Always test the complete flow from connection → authentication → command → response to ensure end-to-end functionality.
